    "searchText": "IBM-041 IBM Research Ponder This 2001-09 Bounds on a permutation group 满足长循环条件的置换群大小 This month's entry is more of a research problem than puzzle. It was originally proposed by Thomas Schwentick. For given N, find upper and lower bounds on the size largest group G permutations N elements (0,1,...,N-1) such that each element g G, when composed with particular N-cycle (0->1->2->...->(N-1)->0), yields another N-cycle. Terminology: set composition any two again in G. A cycle written (a,b,c), meaning (a goes to b, b c, c a). An permutation form (a,b,c,...,h), which cycles through all before returning \"a\". When power 2, we know (2**N)/(2N) exists, as exemplified here N=8. has 2**8/(2*8)=256/16=16 elements. Each represented first row, showing order g(0),g(1),...,g(7), followed traditional notation. 0 1 2 3 4 5 6 7 (0)(1)(2)(3)(4)(5)(6)(7) (0)(1)(2,6)(3,7)(4)(5) (0)(1,5)(2)(3,7)(4)(6) (0)(1,5)(2,6)(3)(4)(7) (0,2)(1,3)(4,6)(5,7) (0,2,4,6)(1,3,5,7) (0,2)(1,7)(3,5)(4,6) (0,2,4,6)(1,7,5,3) (0,4)(1)(2)(3,7)(5)(6) (0,4)(1)(2,6)(3)(5)(7) (0,4)(1,5)(2)(3)(6)(7) (0,4)(1,5)(2,6)(3,7) (0,6,4,2)(1,3,5,7) (0,6)(2,4)(1,3)(5,7) (0,6,4,2)(1,7,5,3) (0,6)(2,4)(1,7)(3,5) As an example law, fourth fifth elements, (0,2,4,6)(1,7,5,3), since (0 maps 2), (1 7), (2 4), (3 1), (4 6), (5 3), (6 0), (7 5). property we're looking for, last 8-cycle (0,1,2,3,4,5,6,7) (0,7,2,5,4,3,6,1). The generalization this \"chandelier group\". We take binary tree, bottom leaves representing integers N-1; top node least significant bit (so left subtree represents even right odd integers), so on. are [0,4,2,6,1,5,3,7] corresponding reverse representation. Group operations those movements tree there number transpositions at (3=log N) levels tree. best bound I about sqrt(N!). Special kudos submitter successive improvement (starting bidding (2**N)/(2N)) or \"substantial\" decrease from (N!).)",
